# Keep the build context small and free of anything secret.
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS MORE THAN IT LOOKS: everything sent to the daemon can end up
# in a layer, and a layer is readable by anyone who can pull the image. `.env`
# is the obvious one, but `.git` carries every value ever committed, which is
# worse: deleting a secret from the working tree does not delete it from
# history.

.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not versioned, mounted at run time instead (see compose.prod.yaml).
data/
logs/
experiments/output/

# The track record is mounted read-only, never copied in: it must stay the one
# on the host, written by the local commands.
track_record/

.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/

notebooks/
scratchpad/
downloaded_files/
*.md
!README.md
